; reduce_integer_model: REDUCE on an integer {0, 1, 2} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; REDUCE writes the Rosenberg reduction of x0 * x1, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which holds only for binary
; variables. On any other domain the same terms encode a different penalty,
; so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has REDUCE raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XQMX r0          ; integer model, k = 3, 4 variables
PUSH 0           ; var_a
PUSH 1           ; var_b
PUSH 1           ; p_aux
REDUCE r0
HALT
